--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE NOTE (no scope narrowing — covenant #2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The manifest record extracted 0 data sources / 0 panels / 0 charts because the web page file
delegates its whole body to imported sub-components (WeekSelector + SummaryHeroCards + DrivingSection
+ ChargingSection + BatteryHealthSection + AlertsSection + WeekOverWeekSummary, themselves built on
HighlightCard / MiniStat / BatteryPill), and its data comes from the useWeeklyDigest hook. Rather than
ship only the 8 formal items, the FULL web composition is reproduced region-for-region, in the same
data + grouping + order:
  • WeekSelector       — prev/next ghost buttons, calendar + week label, "Current" badge (next disabled
                         on the current week).
  • SummaryHeroCards   — 5 highlight cards (Distance / Drives / Energy / Charging Cost / CO2) each with a
                         trend delta, + the conditional Fun-Fact card (closest city-pair comparison).
  • DrivingSection     — daily-distance BAR CHART, 4 mini-stats (Avg Efficiency / Driving Time /
                         Efficiency Change / Drives), Top-Drive card (or its empty state).
  • ChargingSection    — daily-energy BAR CHART, 4 mini-stats (Sessions / Energy Added / Avg Rate /
                         Cost), energy-vs-last-week chip.
  • BatteryHealthSection — 2 battery pills (avg start / end), 3 mini-stats (Charge Gain / Sessions /
                         Est. Range Added).
  • AlertsSection      — count badge, severity breakdown rows + alert-distribution PIE CHART, OR the
                         no-alerts empty state.
  • WeekOverWeekSummary — 6 comparison StatCards (Distance / Drives / Energy / Cost / Efficiency / CO2)
                         each with a color-inverted-where-lower-is-better trend.
Charts use the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers (TSBarChart / TSPieChart inside TSChartContainer) — never
a WKWebView. The opt-in AIDigestNarration block the web page also mounts is wrapped by
withAiFeature('digest-narration', …) and renders as a no-op when AI mode is off; it is its own
cross-cutting AI parity unit (not in this page's manifest record, not among its 5 string keys) and is
explicitly out of scope here — the deterministic digest above is the canonical baseline for every user.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATH NOTE (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated output path (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Analytics/**) does not match the
repo's actual SwiftUI source tree. The shared iOS/macOS app target compiles apps/apple/Sources/**
(project.yml), and every already-DONE sibling P7 analytics page lives under Sources/Features/Analytics/.
A file under TeslaSync/Features/** would NOT be compiled into any target (project.yml has no such source
group). This page therefore ships under apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/** + Tests/Unit/Features/
Analytics/, exactly mirroring the DONE siblings (Analytics / Statistics / FleetCompare / Mileage /
LifetimeStats / TrueCost / PeriodCompare / Timeline / YearReview).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAVIGATION NOTE (no predecessor bypass — covenant #7)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web route /weekly-digest had no AppRoute case. A new `weeklyDigest` case was added (pathSegment
"weekly-digest", group .insights, SF Symbol "calendar" — matching the existing Analytics-overview quick
link `AnalyticsQuickLink(... systemImage: "calendar", path: "/weekly-digest")`). The three exhaustive
AppRoute switches (pathSegment / systemImage / group) were updated; titleKey resolves to the new
route.weeklyDigest string. AppRouteParser needs no alias — /weekly-digest resolves through the
pathSegment fallback. WeeklyDigestRouteRegistration registers .weeklyDigest and is composed into
TeslaSyncApp.swift immediately after StatisticsRouteRegistration. Tests/Unit/App/RouteTests stays green:
its only structural assertion is pathSegment uniqueness, and "weekly-digest" is unique.

